	'k349be30b' => 'Writes home recovery and rehabilitation plans after surgery.',
	'k356f0ae0' => 'Access and hours',
	'k36251d04' => 'A nurse calls within 48 hours. After surgery, pain relief and notes for home recovery go with you on the day, and the discharge call checks how the first night went.',
	'k36b64aad' => 'Diagnostics',
	'k37753395' => 'Vaccinations and prevention',
	'k387e6551' => 'Phone +1 555 0142 300 or email hello@aobavet.example. A first consultation is 30 minutes and includes a full examination. A follow-up consultation is 15 minutes. Say if your animal is a cat, so we can keep the arrival quiet.',
	'k3978195f' => 'Visit the clinic',
	'k3a7ac8ba' => 'A nurse stays with the anaesthetic throughout, watching heart rate, breathing and temperature. We tell you afterwards how that anaesthetic went. Your animal then rests on a soft blanket in a recovery kennel until it is sensible to travel. You are welcome to call the clinic on +1 555 0142 300 if the morning raises a question. The team would rather hear it then than have you guess. Discharge happens only when your animal is ready to leave the building safely.',
	'k3ac640e1' => 'Check-ups, vaccines and care for dogs of every age.',
	'k3c96c494' => 'Bring your cat in a secure carrier, with a familiar towel in the base if you have one. Keep the carrier closed on the journey and speak softly. When you reach 214 Alder Street, the reception desk will point you to the cat waiting room rather than leaving you in a mixed hallway. Clara Moreau, reception and care coordinator, or a nurse, meets you there. We book cat visits so the time in the carrier stays close to the appointment you were given.',
	'k40b75c96' => 'Aoba Veterinary Clinic sees dogs and cats only. The waiting rooms, the handling and the way the day is timed are built for those two, because that is the medicine the team practises every day. Cats have a room of their own, so a carrier is not set down in the middle of dogs. Dogs are examined, admitted and discharged on a path that leaves the cat room quiet.',
	'k412de67f' => '214 Alder Street, Fairhaven',
	'k41d737b3' => 'Card, cash and insurance forms',
	'k422e85fb' => 'A first consultation is 30 minutes and includes a full examination. You are shown what we find, and if treatment is needed you receive a written estimate before it starts. Cats settle in their own waiting room. Within 48 hours a nurse calls to ask how things are going at home. The same people stay with the case from that first conversation through to the follow-up.',
	'k422eaaa2' => 'Seven people, by name',
	'k4332479a' => 'Out of hours, call the regional emergency hospital for a true emergency. When we are open, the filled booking route is this one: phone +1 555 0142 300 or email hello@aobavet.example. The clinic is at 214 Alder Street, Fairhaven, with 6 parking spaces. Aoba Veterinary Clinic has used these hours, this address and this fee list since the practice was founded in 2014. Prices include tax, and the estimate still comes before treatment.',
	'k43394703' => 'Nursing &amp; recovery',
	'k4403e684' => 'Hannah Lindqvist is head veterinary nurse. She leads nursing through examinations, surgery days, recovery and the calls that follow a visit. Malik Haddad is a veterinary nurse in rehabilitation. He wrote the plan that took Biscuit from cruciate surgery to full walks in 10 weeks. Clara Moreau is reception and care coordinator. She books visits, meets you at the desk, and keeps the day in order for dogs and cats alike.',
	'k444f5920' => 'After you email or call, the clinic confirms the day, the time, and whether you are booked for 30 minutes or 15. We say what to bring: the vaccination record, a list of food and medicines, and a photo or video of the symptom if you have one. If a procedure is being planned, we give fasting instructions for that animal. You get a written estimate before treatment, so confirmation of an appointment is not by itself permission to start a procedure.',
	'k47ee9f5c' => 'He did that for Biscuit, a beagle aged 7, after Dr. Osei repaired a cruciate ligament, and Biscuit was on full walks in 10 weeks. That interval belonged to Biscuit. Every animal is different. Call if the wound, the appetite or the comfort is not what the notes led you to expect.',
	'k49ed52bb' => 'Reception and care coordinator',
	'k4ab33428' => 'If you are unsure, call us — a nurse will tell you whether it can wait. You do not need a diagnosis before you phone. Bring a short note of when the sign started, and a photo or video if you have one.',
	'k4c3880bb' => 'Method',
	'k4cc2ab05' => 'Surgery',
	'k4ead77b6' => 'Monday to Friday the clinic is open 9:00–12:30 and 15:30–19:00. Saturday it is open 9:00–12:30 and 15:30–17:00. Saturday afternoon is the shorter session. Sunday and public holidays are closed. We work those two blocks, morning and afternoon, with the middle of the day between them. Appointments are placed inside the open hours.',
	'k503ff0b7' => 'Examine and explain',
	'k53bebca1' => 'Rooms · Surgery · Nursing',
	'k566d3df1' => 'Digital imaging is part of how dentistry is planned here, since dentistry and imaging are his field. Pain relief is on the estimate as well, and it continues as your animal goes home. If the mouth you can see at home looks worse than at the last vaccination, book a consultation first. The $65 first visit, or a $45 follow-up if we have seen your animal recently, is how a dental day is decided.',
	'k575e3871' => 'The figure we put first is $65. That is the first consultation: 30 minutes, with a full examination. It is the visit most new dogs and cats start with, whether the worry is ears, a limp, weight loss, teeth or a vaccination that is due. You get the examination, an explanation of what we find, and a written estimate before any treatment. A shorter return visit, the follow-up consultation of 15 minutes, is $45.',
	'k58121d8a' => 'A first consultation is 30 minutes. A follow-up is 15 minutes. Arriving a few minutes early is enough. If your cat is already worried at home, say so when you book on +1 555 0142 300 and we will keep the arrival as simple as the day allows.',
	'k592ddcb8' => 'Opened in 2014',
	'k5e29c304' => 'Stock, equipment and appointment length follow the same choice. Dr. Varga brought that focus from twelve years of referral work into a general practice she could keep personal. If you share your home with a dog or a cat in Fairhaven, this is the clinic that was arranged for that animal.',
	'k60452be4' => 'He was back on his morning walk by spring.',
	'k619f47cd' => 'Limping that lasts beyond 24 hours',
	'k62335762' => 'Dr. Priya Nair',
